#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: callout"
msgstr ""

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`div[class~=\"instui-callout\"]` — Inline information alert for a short reminder or note."
msgstr "`div[class~=\"instui-callout\"]` — Alèt enfòmasyon anliy pou yon ti rapèl oswa nòt."

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "✅ Use Callout when:"
msgstr "✅ Itilize Callout lè:"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- You need to highlight important information or reminders inline\n- The message is relatively brief (a sentence to a short paragraph)\n- The alert should draw attention without interrupting the main flow\n🚫 Don't use Callout when:"
msgstr "- Ou bezwen mete an evidans enfòmasyon enpòtan oswa rapèl anliy\n- Mesaj la relativman kout (yon fraz oswa yon ti paragraf)\n- Alèt la ta dwe atire atansyon san li pa entèwonp koule prensipal la\n🚫 Pa itilize Callout lè:"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- The message requires interaction or multiple actions — use a Modal or Alert Dialog\n- The content is the main focus of the page — use a Card or Hero layout instead"
msgstr "- Mesaj la mande entèraksyon oswa plizyè aksyon — itilize yon Modal oswa Alert Dialog\n- Kontni an se sant atansyon paj la — itilize yon Card oswa layout Hero olye de sa"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Ensure the alert role is properly applied (role=\"alert\" or role=\"status\")\n- Use semantic color contrast that meets WCAG AA standards\n- Don't rely on color alone to convey meaning"
msgstr "- Asire w wòl alèt la aplike kòrèkteman (role=\"alert\" oswa role=\"status\")\n- Sèvi ak kontrast koulè semantik ki satisfè estanda WCAG AA\n- Pa konte sèlman sou koulè pou transmèt sans"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Alert message content"
msgstr "Kontni mesaj alèt"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container for the text content."
msgstr "Kontenè pou kontni tèks la."

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Optional icon to the left of the content."
msgstr "Ikòn opsyonèl sou bò gòch kontni an."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: card"
msgstr ""

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-card` — A surface container that accepts arbitrary content."
msgstr "`.instui-card` — Yon kontenè sifas ki aksepte kontni o aza."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Variant** controls how direct children are styled: `content` (default) leaves them\n  unstyled; `container` stacks them as bordered, padded sections. Padding scales with\n  viewport width and is the same across both variants.\n  **Size** is fully responsive — padding and border-radius step up automatically at 320px\n  (20rem) and 640px (40rem) via standard `min-width` media queries; no size class is needed.\n  Pair with `@pantoken/components` for heading, button, and other inline components."
msgstr "**Variant** kontwole kijan timoun dirèk yo stilize: `content` (pa defo) kite yo\n  san estil; `container` mete yo youn sou lòt kòm seksyon ak fwontyè ak pad. Pad la adapte ak\n  lajè fenèt navigatè a epi li menm pou toude variant yo.\n  **Gwosè** konplètman reponn — pad ak border-radius ogmante otomatikman nan 320px\n  (20rem) ak 640px (40rem) atravè medya query estanda `min-width`; pa bezwen klas gwosè.\n  Konbine ak `@pantoken/components` pou tit, bouton, ak lòt konpozan anliy."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Use `<article>` as the card element when the card is a self-contained unit of content;\n  use `<section>` when grouped within a larger landmark. In `-variant-container`, prefer\n  `<section>` elements as direct children so each bordered region carries semantic meaning."
msgstr "Sèvi ak `<article>` kòm eleman kat la lè kat la se yon inite kontni endepandan;\n  sèvi ak `<section>` lè li gwoupe andedan yon landmark pi gwo. Nan `-variant-container`, prefere\n  eleman `<section>` kòm timoun dirèk pou chak rejyon gen yon siyifikasyon semantik."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Content card -nocard"
msgstr "Kat kontni -nocard"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container card -nocard"
msgstr "Kat kontenè -nocard"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container card; direct children become bordered, padded sections."
msgstr "Kat kontenè; timoun dirèk vin seksyon ak fwontyè ak pad."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Standard content card; children are unstyled. Default when no variant is set."
msgstr "Kat kontni estanda; timoun yo pa gen estil. Dèfò lè pa gen okenn variant ki mete."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- `@scope` is Baseline 2023 Newly Available; the card degrades to an unscoped flat stylesheet\n  in older browsers with no loss of visible styling."
msgstr "- `@scope` se Baseline 2023 Newly Available; kat la degrade nan yon stylesheet plat san eskòp\n  nan navigatè ki pi ansyen san pèdi estil vizib."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [heading](/api/css/heading.md) — Place directly in the card or inside a container section.\n- [button](/api/css/button.md) — Place directly in the card or inside a container section.\n- [img](/api/css/img.md) — Place directly in the card as a media region.\n- [badge](/api/css/badge.md) — Place directly in the card as a status indicator."
msgstr "- [heading](/api/css/heading.md) — Mete dirèkteman nan kat la oswa anndan yon seksyon kontenè.\n- [button](/api/css/button.md) — Mete dirèkteman nan kat la oswa anndan yon seksyon kontenè.\n- [img](/api/css/img.md) — Mete dirèkteman nan kat la kòm yon rejyon medya.\n- [badge](/api/css/badge.md) — Mete dirèkteman nan kat la kòm yon endikatè estati."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-6/#scoping"
msgstr "- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-6/#scoping"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: checkbox"
msgstr ""

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-checkbox` — A native checkbox and its label, or a switch via `-variant-toggle`."
msgstr "`.instui-checkbox` — Yon checkbox natif natal ak etikèt li, oswa yon switch atravè `-variant-toggle`."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Set `el.indeterminate = true` in JavaScript to show the mixed-state dash; the checked tick auto-contrasts against the fill — white on a dark fill, near-black on a light one. Also sets its own `gap` between the control and its label; chaining a `-gap-*` spacing utility modifier overrides that built-in value."
msgstr "Mete `el.indeterminate = true` nan JavaScript pou montre liy tirè eta-melanje a; tik chèk la fè kontrast otomatik ak ranpli a — blan sou yon ranpli fonse, prèske nwa sou yon ranpli limyè. Li tou mete pwòp `gap` li ant kontwòl la ak etikèt li; chèn yon modifikatè espas `-gap-*` ranplase valè entegre sa a."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [checkbox.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/checkbox/checkbox.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [checkbox.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/checkbox/checkbox.css)"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A native `<input type=\"checkbox\">` drives `:checked`, `:indeterminate`, and `:disabled`; set `el.indeterminate = true` in JavaScript for the mixed state, and note that `-readonly` is styling only since checkboxes have no native readonly attribute."
msgstr "Yon `<input type=\"checkbox\">` natif natal kondwi `:checked`, `:indeterminate`, ak `:disabled`; mete `el.indeterminate = true` nan JavaScript pou eta melanje a, epi sonje ke `-readonly` se sèlman stil paske checkbox yo pa gen atribi readonly natif natal."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Invalid (error) state."
msgstr "Eta ki pa valab (erè)."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Place the label after the control."
msgstr "Plase etikèt la apre kontwòl la."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Place the label before the control."
msgstr "Plase etikèt la anvan kontwòl la."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Place the label above the control."
msgstr "Plase etikèt la anlè kontwòl la."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Read-only state."
msgstr "Eta sèlman-li-lez."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Show the required-field asterisk next to the label."
msgstr "Montre etwal (*) pou chan ki obligatwa a bò etikèt la."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Render as a switch instead of a box."
msgstr "Rann kòm yon switch olye de yon bwat."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The required-field asterisk."
msgstr "Etwal pou chan obligatwa a."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "On `-variant-toggle`, the state glyph riding the handle: an X when off, a check when on."
msgstr "Sou `-variant-toggle`, glif eta ki chita sou manch lan: yon X lè li etenn, yon chèk lè li limen."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The masked tick or dash glyph centered in the box; on `-variant-toggle` it becomes the sliding handle instead."
msgstr "Tik oswa glif tirè kache a santre nan bwat la; sou `-variant-toggle` li vin manch k ap glise a olye."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The box's mask glyph: a tick when checked, a dash when indeterminate."
msgstr "Glif mask bwat la: yon tik lè tcheke, yon tirè lè endetermine."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The toggle border width."
msgstr "Lajè bor toggle la."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The toggle switch height."
msgstr "Wotè switch toggle la."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The computed handle diameter."
msgstr "Dyamèt manch kalkile a."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The handle inset from each track edge."
msgstr "Enset manch la soti nan chak kwen tras la."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The toggle track width."
msgstr "Lajè tras toggle la."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [radio](/api/css/radio.md) — The single-select counterpart."
msgstr "- [radio](/api/css/radio.md) — Konpatriyèl seleksyon-sèl la."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: close-button"
msgstr ""

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-close-button` — A transparent icon button that draws its own × glyph, in three sizes plus an on-color variant."
msgstr "`.instui-close-button` — Yon bouton ikon transparan ki trase pwòp glyf × li, nan twa gwosè plis yon variant sou-koulè."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Always renders as an icon-only control with no visible label, so an `aria-label` is required, not optional; compare to `button`'s `-without-background` ghost variant, which keeps a text label."
msgstr "Toujou rann kòm yon kontwòl sèlman-ikon san okenn etikèt vizib, kidonk yon `aria-label` obligatwa, pa opsyonèl; konpare ak variant fant `-without-background` nan `button`, ki kenbe yon etikèt tèks."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [close-button.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/close-button/close-button.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [close-button.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/close-button/close-button.css)"

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Give the icon-only button an `aria-label` (e.g. \"Close\"), and mark a disabled button with `aria-disabled` (or the native `disabled`)."
msgstr "Bay bouton sèlman-ikon an yon `aria-label` (pa egzanp \"Close\"), epi make yon bouton enfim ak `aria-disabled` (oswa natif `disabled`)."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "For a close button placed on a coloured (non-neutral) surface."
msgstr "Pou yon bouton fèmen ki plase sou yon sifas koulè (ki pa net)."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The × glyph, masked in `currentColor`."
msgstr "Glyf × la, kache nan `currentColor`."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [button](/api/css/button.md) — The general-purpose action button."
msgstr "- [button](/api/css/button.md) — Bouton aksyon jeneral-pou-itilize."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: color"
msgstr ""

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.--text-danger` — Semantic colour utilities: `.--bg-<name>`, `.--text-<name>` (aliased as `.--color-<name>`), and `.--border-<name>` for the curated semantic palette. Every one of these also has a component-attached alias modifier (for example `-bg-danger` on any `.instui-<component>`)."
msgstr "`.--text-danger` — Itilizite koulè semantik: `.--bg-<name>`, `.--text-<name>` (alias `.--color-<name>`), ak `.--border-<name>` pou palèt semantik kiltive. Chak youn nan sa yo gen tou yon modifikatè alias atache ak konpozan (pa egzanp `-bg-danger` sou nenpòt `.instui-<component>`)."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [generate.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/scripts/generate.ts)"
msgstr "**Source:** [generate.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/scripts/generate.ts)"

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Applies the semantic danger text colour."
msgstr "Aplike koulè tèks danje semantik la."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Background colour utilities for semantic and component-aligned names."
msgstr "Itilite koulè background pou non alinye ak semantik ak konpozan."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Border colour utilities for semantic and component-aligned names."
msgstr "Itilite koulè bor pou non alinye ak semantik ak konpozan."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Alias of `--text-*` for text colour utilities."
msgstr "Alias `--text-*` pou itilite koulè tèks."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Text colour utilities for semantic and component-aligned names."
msgstr "Itilite koulè tèks pou non alinye ak semantik ak konpozan."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: context-view"
msgstr ""

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-context-view` — An elevated callout with a caret, positionable on any side; works as a native `[popover]`."
msgstr "`.instui-context-view` — Yon apèl elve ak yon caret, pozisyone sou nenpòt bò; fonksyone kòm yon `[popover]` natif natal."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The caret is two stacked `::before`/`::after` triangles (border then fill) so it reads correctly against a matching surface; as a `[popover]` it needs the same open/`popovertarget` wiring as `popover`, but unlike `tooltip`, it dismisses on outside click or Escape."
msgstr "Caret la se de triyang anpile `::before`/`::after` (bor puis ranpli) konsa li parèt kòrèkteman kont yon sifas ki matche; kòm yon `[popover]` li bezwen menm fil ouvè/`popovertarget` tankou `popover`, men kontrèman ak `tooltip`, li fèmen lè klike deyò oswa peze Escape."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [context-view.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/context-view/context-view.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [context-view.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/context-view/context-view.css)"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Dark (inverse) colour scheme."
msgstr "Sèk koulè fonse (envès)."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit below the anchor."
msgstr "Plase anba ankre a."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit at the end (inline-end) of the anchor."
msgstr "Plase nan fen (inline-end) ankre a."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit at the start (inline-start) of the anchor."
msgstr "Plase nan kòmansman (inline-start) ankre a."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit above the anchor."
msgstr "Plase anlè ankre a."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Renders the caret's inner fill triangle."
msgstr "Rann triyang ranpli entèn caret la."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Renders the caret's outer border triangle."
msgstr "Rann triyang bor ekstèn caret la."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Uses CSS anchor positioning (`position-anchor`, `position-area`, `position-try-fallbacks`) and the native `[popover]` API behind an `@supports` guard; needs a recent Chromium or Safari, and falls back to a UA-centred popover elsewhere."
msgstr "- Itilize pozisyonman anchor CSS (`position-anchor`, `position-area`, `position-try-fallbacks`) ak API natif `[popover]` dèyè yon gad `@supports`; mande yon Chromium oswa Safari resan, epi li tounen sou yon popover santre sou UA lòt kote."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [popover](/api/css/popover.md) — The generic top-layer popover.\n- [tooltip](/api/css/tooltip.md) — A smaller hover or focus callout."
msgstr "- [popover](/api/css/popover.md) — Popover jenerik ki sou kouch siperyè.\n- [tooltip](/api/css/tooltip.md) — Yon ti apèl ki parèt sou hover oswa fokus."

#: css/cursor.md
