#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# Function: onColor()"
msgstr "# Fonksyon: onColor()"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The readable foreground — black or white — for content placed *on* `surface`. This is the CSS-only\nform of InstUI's recurring `*-on-color` variants (a focus ring on a brand button, a\nprimary-inverse button's text, an icon on a coloured surface): rather than a fixed inverse token,\nit picks the contrast from the surface itself, so it stays correct as the surface changes."
msgstr "Tekst devan ki lizib — nwa oswa blan — pou kontni mete *sou* `surface`. Sa a se fòm CSS-sèl nan varyant `*-on-color` InstUI ki repete yo (yon bag fokus sou yon bouton mak, tèks yon bouton primary-inverse, yon ikon sou yon sifas koulè): olye de yon token inverse fiks, li chwazi kontrast la depi nan sifas la menm, konsa li rete kòrèk lè sifas la chanje."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "It reads the surface's OKLCH lightness through relative color syntax and snaps it to `0` (black) or\n`1` (white) at `threshold` using the `calc(… * infinity)` clamp trick — no JS, no fixed hex."
msgstr "Li li klète OKLCH sifas la atravè sentaks koulè relatif epi li kole li sou `0` (nwa) oswa `1` (blan) nan `threshold` lè l sèvi avèk astis `calc(… * infinity)` clamp — pa gen JS, pa gen hex fiks."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "### surface"
msgstr "### surface"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
