msgstr "Konbyen nan `overlay` ki parèt, 0–100 (valè pa defo `50`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# colors"
msgstr "# colors"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — CSS-only color math that mirrors the InstUI `@instructure/ui-color-utils`\nhelpers (`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."
msgstr "`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — matematik koulè sèlman nan CSS ki reflete `@instructure/ui-color-utils` InstUI\nhelpers (`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "InstUI computes those at build time with `tinycolor2` against concrete hex values. pantoken emits\n`var(--instui-*)` references that resolve in the browser (often through `light-dark()`), so the\nmath has to happen in CSS instead. Each helper returns a CSS color string built from\n[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-mix) and\n[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\nboth Baseline modern-browser features — so a single expression tracks the token even when it's a\nscheme-dependent `light-dark()` pair. Use them wherever you'd otherwise hard-code a derived shade."
msgstr "InstUI kalkile sa yo pandan faz build avèk `tinycolor2` kont valè hex konkrè. pantoken emèt\nreferans `var(--instui-*)` ki rezoud nan navigatè a (souvan atravè `light-dark()`), kidonk\nmatematik la dwe fèt nan CSS olye. Chak helper retounen yon chenn koulè CSS ki konstwi soti nan\n[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-mix) ak\n[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\nTou de se karakteristik modèn navigatè Baseline — konsa yon sèl ekspresyon suiv token an menm lè li se yon\npeye `light-dark()` depandan sou chema. Sèvi ak yo kote ou ta sinon kòd di yon ton derive."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/type-aliases/CssColor.md
